ember:429898651":{"__typename":"Member","id":"429898651","name":"Alexander Turner","memberPhoto":{"__ref":"PhotoInfo:320986337"}},"Member:485315212":{"__typename":"Member","id":"485315212","name":"Celina","memberPhoto":{"__ref":"PhotoInfo:326665489"}},"Member:484094614":{"__typename":"Member","id":"484094614","name":"alexsvhsu","memberPhoto":null},"Member:100784562":{"__typename":"Member","id":"100784562","name":"coban Tun","memberPhoto":{"__ref":"PhotoInfo:232736212"}},"Member:426247694":{"__typename":"Member","id":"426247694","name":"Cameron Mau","memberPhoto":null},"Event:317172030":{"__typename":"Event","id":"317172030","dateTime":"2026-11-30T19:30:00-08:00","isAttending":false,"group":{"__typename":"Group","urlname":"noisebridge","__ref":"Group:19346164"},"title":"Mozzi On Arduino (Circuit Hacking Mondays)","description":"Mozzi is a library of audio functions that run on Arduino and ESP 32\nmicroprocessors.\n\nMozzi is a well documented collection of audio programs with example sketches, detailed notes and a support community. I first heard about Mozzi on the Noisebridge-Discord pedal building channel. The Arduino/Mozzi system is a popular platform for making custom guitar effects pedals and synth modules. This CHM workshop presents the Mozzi/Arduino setup, a simple sound production circuit (transistor amplifier and speaker) and runs through some of the examples provided through the Arduino iDE.\n\nContinuing where we left off but come anyway if you missed the first class.","eventType":"PHYSICAL","eventUrl":"https://www.meetup.com/noisebridge/events/317172030/","isSaved":false,"maxTickets":0,"rsvpState":"JOIN_OPEN","featuredEventPhoto":{"__ref":"PhotoInfo:537181154"},"displayPhoto":{"__ref":"PhotoInfo:537181154"},"feeSettings":null,"socialProofInsights":{"__typename":"SocialProofInsights","isTrendingEvent":false,"totalInterestedUsers":45,"interestedUsersSample":[{"__typename":"Member","memberPhoto":{"__ref":"PhotoInfo:326568813"}},{"__typename":"Member","member